# pinchtask

> [!WARNING]
> Almost all code is generated by GLM-5-Turbo. This program is provided as-is without any warranty.

Providing structured task management capabilities for AI Agent and human collaboration.

Supports three usage modes: **CLI local operations**, **TUI**, and **MCP server**, all sharing the same core business logic and data storage.

[中文文档](README.md)

## Features

- **Task Management** — Create, view, edit, and delete tasks with descriptions and shared context
- **Checklist System** — Each task contains ordered checklist items with full CRUD, mark complete/incomplete, and reordering
- **Notes** — Append free-form text notes to tasks
- **Resource References** — Link external documents, URLs, or file paths
- **Project Management** — Create, view, edit, and delete projects with task association (one-to-many)
- **Metadata** — Tags, priority (high/medium/low), and estimated completion time
- **Short ID Matching** — CLI supports entering the first 4+ characters of a UUID to locate tasks
- **Dual Mode** — Direct CLI operations / MCP stdio server for AI Agent invocation
- **JSON Output** — All query commands support the `--json` flag for machine-readable output
- **Interactive TUI** — Terminal interface based on ratatui with keyboard navigation, real-time search, and task management
- **Workspace Association** — Automatically associate projects via `.pinchproject` file, supported across CLI/TUI/MCP

## Installation

### Build from Source

```bash
# Requires Rust 1.88+ and Cargo
git clone https://github.com/Raven-1027/pinchtask.git
cd pinchtask
cargo build --release
# Binary is located at target/release/pinchtask
```

### Install via Cargo

```bash
cargo install --git https://github.com/Raven-1027/pinchtask
```

## Quick Start

### Create and Manage a Task

```bash
# Create a task
pinchtask task new "Implement user login" -c "Use JWT authentication"

# View task list
pinchtask task ls

# Add a checklist item
pinchtask item add <TASK_ID> "Design database schema" -d "users table and sessions table"

# Mark item as complete
pinchtask item check <TASK_ID> 0

# View progress summary
pinchtask item summary <TASK_ID>

# View task details
pinchtask task show <TASK_ID>
```

### Start MCP Server

```bash
# Run directly (auto-enters server mode when no subcommand is given)
pinchtask

# Or explicitly specify
pinchtask serve
```

### Workspace Project Association

Create a `.pinchproject` file in your project root directory containing the project UUID:

```bash
# First create a project
pinchtask project new "My Project"

# Create .pinchproject file in the project root
echo "PROJECT_UUID" > .pinchproject
```

When running `task new`, `task ls`, and other commands from this directory (or any subdirectory), tasks are automatically associated with that project. Explicit `--project` flag always takes priority.

## CLI Usage

```
pinchtask [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Global options:
  -D, --data-dir <DIR>      Data storage directory (default: ~/.pinchtask)
      --log-level <LEVEL>   Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
  -v, --verbose             Verbose output (equivalent to --log-level debug)
  -q, --quiet               Quiet mode (equivalent to --log-level error)
      --json                Output in JSON format

Commands:
  task        Task management (new, ls, show, edit, rm)
  item        Checklist item management (add, check, mv, summary, edit, rm)
  note        Note management (add, rm)
  link        Resource reference management (add, rm)
  project     Project management (new, ls, show, edit, rm, add-task, rm-task)
  serve       Start MCP server
  completion  Generate shell completion scripts
```

> For full command parameter details, see the [CLI Reference](docs/en/cli.md).

## MCP Configuration

Configure in MCP-compatible AI clients (such as Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pinchtask": {
      "command": "pinchtask",
      "args": ["serve"],
      "env": {
        "PINCHTASK_DATA_DIR": "/path/to/data"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> For full MCP tool details, see the [MCP Protocol Documentation](docs/en/mcp.md).

## TUI Interactive Interface

Launch the terminal-based interactive interface via `pinchtask tui` and manage tasks using keyboard shortcuts.

### Launch

```bash
pinchtask tui
# Or specify a data directory
pinchtask tui -D /path/to/data
```

If a `.pinchproject` file exists in the current directory or any parent directory, the TUI automatically selects the corresponding project on startup.

> For full shortcuts and view details, see the [TUI Documentation](docs/en/tui.md).

## Data Storage

Task data is stored in a SQLite database file:

```
~/.pinchtask/
└── tasks.db
```

The database uses a hybrid normalization design: the `tasks` main table stores basic task information, `checklist_items`, `notes`, and `resources` are separate associated tables, and `metadata` is stored as a JSON column. The data directory can be customized via the `-D` parameter or the `PINCHTASK_DATA_DIR` environment variable. Tasks and projects have a one-to-many relationship — each task belongs to at most one project (via the `tasks.project_id` foreign key), and deleting a project automatically dissociates its tasks.

## Developer Guide

### Build & Test

```bash
cargo build
cargo test                # Run all unit tests
cargo test -- --nocapture # Show println! output
```

